---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '~/components/PageHeader.astro';
import Section from '~/components/Section.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '~/config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How this website is built to be usable with a keyboard, a screen reader, magnification or reduced motion, and how to tell us about a barrier."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Accessibility"
    title="Accessibility statement"
    lead="This site is built to WCAG 2.2 Level AA. If something here does not work for you, we want to hear about it."
  />

  <Section>
    <div class="prose-site">
      <h2>What we have done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Every page works with a keyboard alone, with a visible focus
          indicator that is never removed.
        </li>
        <li>
          Text meets or exceeds a 4.5:1 contrast ratio against its background,
          in both the light and dark colour schemes.
        </li>
        <li>
          Headings, landmarks and lists are real HTML elements, so screen
          readers can navigate the structure.
        </li>
        <li>
          The FAQ uses native disclosure elements rather than scripted
          accordions.
        </li>
        <li>
          Form fields have permanent visible labels, errors are described in
          text next to the field they belong to, and the form works with
          JavaScript turned off.
        </li>
        <li>
          Spam protection is invisible rather than a visual puzzle, so it does
          not become a barrier.
        </li>
        <li>
          Animation is minimal and honours the reduced-motion preference.
        </li>
        <li>
          Tap targets are at least 44 by 44 pixels, and text reflows to 320
          pixels wide without horizontal scrolling.
        </li>
        <li>
          The site follows your system light or dark preference, and text can
          be zoomed to 200 percent without loss of content.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where we know we fall short</h2>
      <p>
        We test with a keyboard, with automated checks and at mobile widths,
        but we have not yet completed testing with every assistive technology.
        If you hit a barrier, that is a defect and we will fix it.
      </p>

      <h2>Tell us</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a> or call
        <a href={CONTACT.phoneHref}>{CONTACT.phone}</a>. Tell us the page and
        what went wrong, and we will respond and let you know what we have
        done. If you cannot use the inquiry form, call or email us and we will
        take your details that way instead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
